course: dictionary
lesson: 15170
title: Sound words that show action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they describe. Screeching is one of them: say it out loud and it sounds high and harsh, like something rubbing or crying out. «The bus stopped with screeching brakes outside the school.» The brakes made a loud, high, rough noise, so screeching describes that sound.
explain: Screeching can also describe a sound that is loud and startling. «A screeching owl woke Maya in the middle of the night.» An owl's cry that is harsh and high, not soft, makes her jump. Ask yourself: is the sound loud, high and rough?
explain: Screeching appears in the phrase «come to a screeching halt». Here the word is not about noise. It tells you the stop was very sudden. «The bike came to a screeching halt when the dog ran into the road.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "loud, high and harsh" in place of screeching in «The seagulls were screeching over the harbour». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Screeching means making a loud, high, harsh sound, like a scream.
fact: «Screeching» can describe brakes or tyres that make a high, rough noise when they stop suddenly.
fact: Screeching can also be a noun, meaning a loud, harsh, high noise.
fact: «Come to a screeching halt» means stop very suddenly.
fact: Screech, screeches, screeched and screeching are all forms of the same word.
exercise: «The bus came to a screeching halt at the zebra crossing.» What does screeching halt mean? | Stopped for a long, quiet rest | *Stopped very suddenly | Went slowly around the corner | Drove away singing
exercise: «We heard screeching tyres as the car turned too fast.» What made the screeching sound? | The bird on the roof | The rain on the window | The school bell | *The tyres
exercise: «The seagulls were screeching over the harbour.» What does screeching mean here? | Singing a soft song | Sleeping peacefully | *Making loud, harsh, high cries | Flying very slowly
test: «The chalk made a screeching noise across the board.» Which sound is screeching like? | A gentle drip | A deep rumble | *A harsh, high squeak | A soft hum
test: Jamie says screeching means quiet and soft. Is he right? | It is a kind of food | It means happy and calm | Yes, it means quiet and soft | *No, it means loud, high and harsh
exam: «The screeching owl startled the village, and the car came to a screeching halt.» Which two meanings does screeching have in this sentence? | Happy singing and a long sleep | Loud laughter and a long walk | A soft sound and a slow movement | *A loud, harsh noise and a sudden stop
